    "master_seed": 20261019,
    "sim_seed": "Every P4 batch run gets its own Gazebo seed (gz sim --seed): first 31 bits of sha256(batch prefix + run id + master_seed), recorded in plan.json, config.json and the Gazebo command line. Gazebo sensor noise (IMU, barometer, magnetometer) is drawn from this seed; without --seed it is drawn from std::random_device.",
    "initial_yaw": {
      "range_deg": [
        -20.0,
        20.0
      ],
      "conditions": [],
      "rule": "P6 draws no random heading: every run spawns at yaw 0 (PX4 heading 96.0 deg).",
      "heading_at_zero_deg": 96.0,
      "heading_rule": "Gazebo yaw is counter-clockwise from East (ENU); PX4 heading is clockwise from North (NED) incl. the world magnetic declination. At spawn yaw 0 the PX4 heading is 96.0 deg (P3 batch-01 first C->N 95.99-96.05 deg; P4 dev-01 95.9 deg), so the expected heading before arming is 96.0 - initial_yaw_deg (tolerance 3 deg)."
    },
    "hover_point": "Not perturbed: the local frame origin is the spawn point and the Gazebo world is flat and translation invariant, so a horizontal offset of the hover point changes nothing the controllers or the physics see; the hover altitude stays the frozen 3 m (analysis references).",
    "verification": "Before the batches: (1) startup-only runs with seeds A, A, B compare the at-rest raw gyro noise (sensor_gyro) sample by sample: same seed identical, different seed different; (2) development flights with different seeds/headings give different measured values; (3) every batch run checks that its Gazebo command carried the planned seed and that the heading at takeoff equals the planned heading (tolerance 3 deg).",
    "default_settings": "Every P6 batch run (incl. the equivalence) gets its own Gazebo seed."
  },
